{"LHIN_Label_Text2":"North East Region","OrgCategory_Label_Text2":"Small Hospital","formatted_current_value2":"75.00","formatted_progress_value2":"57.60","formatted_target_value2":"161.00","measure_header_Text2":"Number of workplace violence incidents reported by hospital workers (as defined by OHSA) within a 12 month period.","methods":"Y","org_name_Text2":"Sault Area Hospital","planned_initiative":"Implement 3 high priority initiatives that focus on delirium reduction.","process_measure":"The Clinical Directors of Medicine, Allied Health, and Geriatrics have 
established a hospital elder life program (HELP) model of care that greatly benefits patients who present with delirium or have high risk of delirium.

Work is underway to develop referral pathways to facilitate early identification and access to HELP. Geriatric department has purchased a two-year subscription to the “AGS CoCare HELP Program”. This subscription provides access to the full portfolio of tools and resources, providing our organization with everything needed to implement the HELP program.","progress2":"","sector_name_Text2":"Acute Care/Hospital"}

{"LHIN_Label_Text2":"Toronto Region","OrgCategory_Label_Text2":"Specialty Children Hospital","formatted_current_value2":"CB","formatted_progress_value2":"40.00","formatted_target_value2":"21.00","measure_header_Text2":"Optimize the inpatient experience survey response rate using Qualtrics software?","methods":"Y","org_name_Text2":"Hospital for Sick Children (The)","planned_initiative":"A SickKids email address is being utilized to distribute surveys. This measure is taken to provide patients/families with assurance that the survey invitation originates from the hospital and is legitimate.","process_measure":"Response rate has consistently surpassed the target, suggesting that use of a SickKids email domain has been a successful change idea 

Use of a SickKids email domain does not eliminate the possibility of email invites going to Junk folders. The percentage of email invites opened and viewed has consistently been within the 60%-70% range, and there has been some recipient feedback about missing the email. 

 Additional verbal communication to patients/families to check their email inboxes and ensure SickKids is on their ‘safe senders’ list is advised.","progress2":"","sector_name_Text2":"Acute Care/Hospital"}

{"LHIN_Label_Text2":"Toronto Region","OrgCategory_Label_Text2":"Specialty Children Hospital","formatted_current_value2":"CB","formatted_progress_value2":"40.00","formatted_target_value2":"21.00","measure_header_Text2":"Optimize the inpatient experience survey response rate using Qualtrics software?","methods":"Y","org_name_Text2":"Hospital for Sick Children (The)","planned_initiative":"The sampling method for inpatient units has been altered. The shift has been made from a stratified sampling approach to a census sampling approach. Under the stratified sampling method, surveys were distributed to a specific number of families/caregivers within each inpatient unit. However, with census sampling, every eligible individual discharged from an inpatient unit receives an invitation to participate in the survey.","process_measure":"Census sampling is an effective approach to increase the response rate and volume of responses across the inpatient areas 

Additional approaches are needed to ensure individual inpatient areas have representative sample sizes  

There is an opportunity to learn from other organizations and consider shortening the quarantine period from 12 months to an alternate period","progress2":"","sector_name_Text2":"Acute Care/Hospital"}

