{"LHIN_Label_Text2":"Toronto Region","OrgCategory_Label_Text2":"Teaching Hospital","formatted_current_value2":"44.90","formatted_progress_value2":"42.20","formatted_target_value2":"36.50","measure_header_Text2":"90th percentile ED length of stay","methods":"Y","org_name_Text2":"University Health Network","planned_initiative":"1. Tracking Time from "Bed Empty" to "New Patient in Bed" (Goal ~90 Mins) 2. Optimization of Access & Flow Meetings 3. Increase Use of Capacity Management Dashboard 4. Optimized Models of Care","process_measure":"Overall, Capacity management efforts to balance the demands for beds, including both scheduled and emergent care, have been ongoing. When appropriate The use of non-conventional spaces to house patients has helped manage capacity effectively.

GIM patients were aligned to specific units, reducing the need for travel between units and fostering stronger team-based care. 

System-level pressures continue to add to challenges for TW and TG sites meeting their targets.","progress2":"UHN has launched a steering committee to advance Ontario Health Home First directives.","sector_name_Text2":"Acute Care/Hospital"}

{"LHIN_Label_Text2":"West Region","OrgCategory_Label_Text2":"Teaching Hospital","formatted_current_value2":"68.90","formatted_progress_value2":"67.80","formatted_target_value2":"80.00","measure_header_Text2":"Percent discharge summaries sent from hospital to community care provider within 48 hours of discharge","methods":"N","org_name_Text2":"London Health Sciences Centre","planned_initiative":"Establish a Resident Quality Council","process_measure":"Given the rotating nature of the resident program, residents have provided feedback that a council focused on standardizing organizational practices across departments would be beneficial. The proposed idea was to establish a resident council that could better interpret data related to discharge summaries and develop standardized strategies for improvement that could be implemented organization wide.

Lessons Learned 
Due to organizational changes this year, there was no sponsorship for this initiative. For a new resident council to be successfully implemented, it is essential to engage key partners who recognize the value of the initiative. LHSC was unable to test this concept this year.","progress2":"","sector_name_Text2":"Acute Care/Hospital"}

