{"LHIN_Label_Text2":"West Region","OrgCategory_Label_Text2":"Large Community Hospital","formatted_current_value2":"5.23","formatted_progress_value2":"5.40","formatted_target_value2":"4.40","measure_header_Text2":"90th percentile emergency department wait time to physician initial assessment","methods":"Y","org_name_Text2":"Chatham-Kent Health Alliance","planned_initiative":"Optimize physician and nurse practitioner schedules to support PIA according to daily capacity and patient acuity trends.","process_measure":"Staffing Trials: Two key trials were conducted to decrease wait times and expedite care: 

RPN Extensions: Lengthened RPN hours to better support medical directives right at triage. 



NP Integration: Temporarily added Nurse Practitioner hours to collaborate with RPNs and Physicians, allowing for initial assessments of patients still in the waiting room.","progress2":"CKHA will continue to use this indicator for the 2026-2027 QIP to build on what has been started and the work that needs to continue to see an improvement in this metric. Additional formal activities will begin in 2026-27 to further support this priority.","sector_name_Text2":"Acute Care/Hospital"}

{"LHIN_Label_Text2":"West Region","OrgCategory_Label_Text2":"Large Community Hospital","formatted_current_value2":"CB","formatted_progress_value2":"93.00","formatted_target_value2":"CB","measure_header_Text2":"Did patients feel they were treated with courtesy and respect during their hospital visit and/or stay?","methods":"N","org_name_Text2":"Chatham-Kent Health Alliance","planned_initiative":"Expand Patient Advisor program to increase patient/family involvement in hospital committees and initiatives.","process_measure":"Actively recruiting new advisors through various forums.  

No official new members onboarded, 2 prospective new Patient Experience Advisors. 



The Quality Committee of the Board, EDIAR council, Accessibility Council, Strategic Planning Committee,  Alliance Awards of Excellence, along with other ad hoc working groups have representation from Patient Experience Advisors. Patient Experience Advisors were also involved in launch of Qualtrics Patient Experience Surveys, participated in Mock Code Simulations, and Renovation projects.","progress2":"CKHA will continue to monitor responses to this specific question from our Patient Experience Survey, however for the 2026-27 QIP, we have decided to group this question with other questions to create a custom "theme" and will be monitoring and working to improve this in more detail.","sector_name_Text2":"Acute Care/Hospital"}

{"LHIN_Label_Text2":"West Region","OrgCategory_Label_Text2":"Large Community Hospital","formatted_current_value2":"CB","formatted_progress_value2":"93.00","formatted_target_value2":"CB","measure_header_Text2":"Did patients feel they were treated with courtesy and respect during their hospital visit and/or stay?","methods":"Y","org_name_Text2":"Chatham-Kent Health Alliance","planned_initiative":"Implement Qualtrics Patient Experience surveys across hospital in and outpatient departments.","process_measure":"Qualtrics Patient Experience surveys are rolled out across most inpatient areas and select outpatient areas of the hospital. Work is underway to expand the areas surveys are being distributed which will include Inpatient Mental Health and Outpatient areas such as Ambulatory Care, Lab and DI. We are facing challenges with the process to gain consent from patients when registering and are working with a regional team to streamline this process and increase the number of patients consenting to receive the survey and provide CKHA with their email addresses at registration. 



Results from the Courtesy and Respect questions are provided to the Quality Committee of the Board and leadership on a quarterly basis. As of Q3, CKHA’s performance on this survey question is that 92.9% of respondents respond positively (top two box) to this question. 



Dashboards are live to the leadership team to view results, and comments provided by patients through the Patient Experience Surveys. Further optimization is underway to refine these dashboards.","progress2":"CKHA will continue to monitor responses to this specific question from our Patient Experience Survey, however for the 2026-27 QIP, we have decided to group this question with other questions to create a custom "theme" and will be monitoring and working to improve this in more detail.","sector_name_Text2":"Acute Care/Hospital"}

{"LHIN_Label_Text2":"West Region","OrgCategory_Label_Text2":"Large Community Hospital","formatted_current_value2":"2.85","formatted_progress_value2":"2.97","formatted_target_value2":"3.05","measure_header_Text2":"Perception of Care Indicator  - Mental Health Patient Experience","methods":"N","org_name_Text2":"Hotel-Dieu Grace Healthcare","planned_initiative":"Implement the revised staffing model as part of the TNI Transformation. 2. Develop and implement standardized processes and workflows with new and existing staffing roles/designations to attach patients to relevant group programming (therapeutic based on presenting diagnosis and elective based on voiced needs and interest) as part of the TNI Transformation. 3. Provide and track relevant staff education."","process_measure":"Progress has been made on the OPOC but not to the degree that we wanted.  However, there was a lag in getting all staff onboarded and trained.  As staff settle into the new roles and processes are solidified we may see some better progress.  We are working on the education strategy development

Positions have all been introduced now after a delay in onboarding. Currently assessing staff engagement through surveys.  An education strategy is being built to be able to track staff education hours. 

Lesson learned was that the education strategy could have been built earlier  on in the project when completely the staff engagement and when introducing the new roles.","progress2":"This indicator will continue on the 26-27 QIP and we will continue to work towards our target and continued progress on action plan.","sector_name_Text2":"Acute Care/Hospital"}

{"LHIN_Label_Text2":"West Region","OrgCategory_Label_Text2":"Large Community Hospital","formatted_current_value2":"7.50","formatted_progress_value2":"7.80","formatted_target_value2":"5.00","measure_header_Text2":"Readmission Rates within 90 days - Mental Health ( TNI )","methods":"N","org_name_Text2":"Hotel-Dieu Grace Healthcare","planned_initiative":"Develop and implement standardized processes and workflows with new and existing staffing roles/designations to attach patients to relevant group programming; 1) Therapeutic based on presenting diagnosis and 2) Elective based on voiced patient needs and interest as part of the TNI Transformation. Ensure consistent and comprehensive transition plans with warm handoffs.","process_measure":"Work was delayed but is now on track and being implemented one designation at a time. Continue to develop and implement standardized processes and workflows for new roles and designations for group programming.  This work is ongoing from last quarter.  
Data quality issues impaired using the data we were capturing.  This is now resolved and we have one quarter of baseline data. Continue to monitor number of group session and group participants. 

Our lessons learned :We could have ensured the data we planned to use for this could be captured and be of good quality before and during the change project.  This also would have required the staff to be trained in how to enter information so it reflected what we wanted to measure.  The target for the process measure should have been a target that could be measured on a more frequent interval, like "Groups per week" - how it is currently written is more like an outcome measure, Groups per fiscal year.","progress2":"This indicator will continue on the 26-27 QIP to ensure we continue to work towards our target and complete implementation of our strategies identified in 25-26.  This work is linked to our ongoing evaluation of our Model of Care Changes in this program.","sector_name_Text2":"Acute Care/Hospital"}

