{"LHIN_Label_Text2":"East Region","OrgCategory_Label_Text2":"Large Community Hospital","aim_header_Text2":"Equitable","comments2":"","current_value_text2":"CB","datasource_period_Text2":"Staff survey / Most recent consecutive 12 month period","goal2":"Q1: 100% Q2: 25% Q3: 60% Q4: 80%","measure_header_Text2":"Survey Question: “On a scale 1-10, where 10 is the highest knowledge, how would you rate your knowledge base regarding the provision of culturally sensitive care?”","methods2":"Identify and select appropriate education programs. Select population for completion of training(s). Establish a method for tracking training progress among staff, and physicians. Implement the new education program(s).","objective_header_Text2":"Equity","org_name_Text2":"Pembroke Regional Hospital Inc.","planned3":"Improve the knowledge, through training/education, of Indigenous culture and health care gaps, and how to reduce disparities.","process_measure3":"Q1: Indigenous cultural training programs identified. Target group for training identified. Q2: Number of employees from target group who have completed the Indigenous cultural training. Q3: Number of employees from target group who have completed the Indigenous cultural training. Q4: Number of employees from target group who have completed the Indigenous cultural training.","sector_name_Text2":"Acute Care/Hospital","target_justification2":"Creating a welcoming, inviting hospital to work in, or receive care is important to achieve better outcomes for workers and patients.  



