{"LHIN_Label_Text2":"Toronto Region","OrgCategory_Label_Text2":"Chronic/Rehab Hospital","aim_header_Text2":"Safe","comments2":"","current_value_text2":"CB","datasource_period_Text2":"Other / 2025-26","goal2":"(1) By June 30, 2025 (2) By September 30, 2025","measure_header_Text2":"Percentage of reduction in new hospital-acquired Stage III & IV Pressure injuries","methods2":"- Interprofessional working group established for all change ideas; meeting agenda to include current state assessment of strategies and gap analysis when applicable - Unit-based forums leveraged to engage point-of-care staff (for example, weekly interprofessional improvement huddles, ETL meetings) - Gap analysis presented at Nursing Practice Affairs Committee for feedback","objective_header_Text2":"Safety","org_name_Text2":"Baycrest Hospital (North York)","planned3":"Develop a sustainability plan and process to monitor mobilization and repositioning strategies","process_measure3":"(1) Gap analysis completed on all 3 Complex Continuing Care units (2) Areas of focus prioritized and action plan developed with timelines and leads","sector_name_Text2":"Acute Care/Hospital","target_justification2":"Baycrest will continue its focus on pressure injury prevention. To align with Never Event Reporting, the indicator will now focus on Stage III & IV pressure injuries acquired in real-time at Baycrest. 

Historically, the indicator measured pressure injuries acquired through point-in-time quarterly prevalence and incidence studies on the following units: Complex Continuing Care units, Transitional Care Unit and Slow Stream Rehabilitation Unit. The 2025-26 indicator aims to capture real-time pressure injury data across all inpatient units.

In parallel, data from the incidence studies will also be used to validate this new indicator (understanding that the incidence studies only reflect pressure injuries from a snapshot in time).","target_value_text2":"CB","unit_population_Text2":"% / Other"}

{"LHIN_Label_Text2":"Toronto Region","OrgCategory_Label_Text2":"Chronic/Rehab Hospital","aim_header_Text2":"Safe","comments2":"","current_value_text2":"CB","datasource_period_Text2":"Other / 2025-26","goal2":"(1) By April 30, 2025 (2) By June 30, 2025 (3) By July 30, 2025 (4) By August 30, 2025","measure_header_Text2":"Percentage of reduction in new hospital-acquired Stage III & IV Pressure injuries","methods2":"- Collaboration with SERS administrator on current reporting form requirements - Communication plan presented and approved at interprofessional working group - Existing visual management system leveraged at improvement huddles to review data on incidents reported - Monthly review of events reported incorporated into the interprofessional working group agenda - Unit leadership discuss learnings at huddles from events reported","objective_header_Text2":"Safety","org_name_Text2":"Baycrest Hospital (North York)","planned3":"Implement reporting of pressure injuries as safety events in the Safety Event Reporting System (SERS)","process_measure3":"(1) Event reporting form finalized (2) Communication plan developed and integrated into practice (3) Monthly SERS incidents posted on each unit (4) First monthly review of incidents by interprofessional working group","sector_name_Text2":"Acute Care/Hospital","target_justification2":"Baycrest will continue its focus on pressure injury prevention. To align with Never Event Reporting, the indicator will now focus on Stage III & IV pressure injuries acquired in real-time at Baycrest. 

Historically, the indicator measured pressure injuries acquired through point-in-time quarterly prevalence and incidence studies on the following units: Complex Continuing Care units, Transitional Care Unit and Slow Stream Rehabilitation Unit. The 2025-26 indicator aims to capture real-time pressure injury data across all inpatient units.

In parallel, data from the incidence studies will also be used to validate this new indicator (understanding that the incidence studies only reflect pressure injuries from a snapshot in time).","target_value_text2":"CB","unit_population_Text2":"% / Other"}

{"LHIN_Label_Text2":"Toronto Region","OrgCategory_Label_Text2":"Chronic/Rehab Hospital","aim_header_Text2":"Safe","comments2":"","current_value_text2":"CB","datasource_period_Text2":"Other / 2025-26","goal2":"(1) By April 30, 2025 (2) By September 30, 2025","measure_header_Text2":"Percentage of reduction in new hospital-acquired Stage III & IV Pressure injuries","methods2":"- Clinical rounds to include standard work on how to flag and action on active pressure injuries on the unit - Leverage clinical report that outlines real-time wounds active on each unit","objective_header_Text2":"Safety","org_name_Text2":"Baycrest Hospital (North York)","planned3":"Implement standardized approaches for interprofessional review of new pressure injuries","process_measure3":"(1) Pilot discussion of new pressure injuries on one Complex Continuing Care (CCC) unit (2) Spread standardized approach to all CCC units","sector_name_Text2":"Acute Care/Hospital","target_justification2":"Baycrest will continue its focus on pressure injury prevention. To align with Never Event Reporting, the indicator will now focus on Stage III & IV pressure injuries acquired in real-time at Baycrest. 

Historically, the indicator measured pressure injuries acquired through point-in-time quarterly prevalence and incidence studies on the following units: Complex Continuing Care units, Transitional Care Unit and Slow Stream Rehabilitation Unit. The 2025-26 indicator aims to capture real-time pressure injury data across all inpatient units.

In parallel, data from the incidence studies will also be used to validate this new indicator (understanding that the incidence studies only reflect pressure injuries from a snapshot in time).","target_value_text2":"CB","unit_population_Text2":"% / Other"}

{"LHIN_Label_Text2":"Toronto Region","OrgCategory_Label_Text2":"Teaching Hospital","aim_header_Text2":"Patient-centred","comments2":"","current_value_text2":"27.00","datasource_period_Text2":"In house data collection  / April 1 2025- March 31, 2026","goal2":"1. 75% of eligible PCMs, operations directors and physician leaders engaged 2. 50% of eligible PCMs, operations directors and physician leaders participate in focus groups","measure_header_Text2":"The percentage of leaders that access the Patient Experience (PE)PowerBI dashboards per month based on the Ontario Hospital Association’s (OHA) digital patient experience surveys.","methods2":"Optimization of dashboard functionality and workflow will be led by the Office of the Patient Experience’s Digital Patient Experience Survey lead with support from Decision Support (DS). This will require: 1. Engagement with leaders and other staff accessing dashboards to optimize functionality to incentivize engagement with the dashboards 2. Engagement with leaders regarding optimal workflow for disseminating the dashboards 3. Create a Dashboard Overview for Patient Care Managers (PCMs) that includes Patient Experience Scores Ensuring meaningful and useful presentation of data via acting on feedback from teams and making iterative modifications to dashboards","objective_header_Text2":"Experience","org_name_Text2":"Sunnybrook Health Sciences Centre","planned3":"Optimize Patient Experience (PE) PowerBI dashboards.","process_measure3":"1. Number of leaders accessing PowerBI dashboards 2. Focus group development and engagement 3. Iterative changes to the dashboards based on feedback gathered","sector_name_Text2":"Acute Care/Hospital","target_justification2":"This indicator is a process measure. In order for patient experience data to effectively lead to improved patient safety and quality of care, the first step is to ensure that those able to effect change are receiving data and viewing the data. 

Therefore, the justification of the target is as a fidelity measure, we need to ensure that all leaders that have an available dashboard are viewing it – and if not, we need to understand why not – to better incorporate it into their workflow. 

Based on last year’s performance, the target of 75% is a stretch target, but anything below that will make it hard for the information available in the patient experience surveys to eventually lead to meaningful change.","target_value_text2":"75.00","unit_population_Text2":"% / Staff"}

{"LHIN_Label_Text2":"Toronto Region","OrgCategory_Label_Text2":"Teaching Hospital","aim_header_Text2":"Patient-centred","comments2":"","current_value_text2":"27.00","datasource_period_Text2":"In house data collection  / April 1 2025- March 31, 2026","goal2":"1. Have the first iteration of operations director/Chief based dashboards available by Q1 (April-June) 2. 100% of eligible operations directors and Chiefs engaged","measure_header_Text2":"The percentage of leaders that access the Patient Experience (PE)PowerBI dashboards per month based on the Ontario Hospital Association’s (OHA) digital patient experience surveys.","methods2":"Creation and implementation will continue to be led jointly by the Office of the Patient Experience’s Digital Patient Experience Survey lead and Decision Support (DS).","objective_header_Text2":"Experience","org_name_Text2":"Sunnybrook Health Sciences Centre","planned3":"Create Program-Specific Dashboards for Operations Directors and Chiefs incorporated into their PowerBI Program dashboards","process_measure3":"1. Number of operations directors and Chiefs reached 2. Iterative changes to the dashboards based on feedback gathered","sector_name_Text2":"Acute Care/Hospital","target_justification2":"This indicator is a process measure. In order for patient experience data to effectively lead to improved patient safety and quality of care, the first step is to ensure that those able to effect change are receiving data and viewing the data. 

Therefore, the justification of the target is as a fidelity measure, we need to ensure that all leaders that have an available dashboard are viewing it – and if not, we need to understand why not – to better incorporate it into their workflow. 

Based on last year’s performance, the target of 75% is a stretch target, but anything below that will make it hard for the information available in the patient experience surveys to eventually lead to meaningful change.","target_value_text2":"75.00","unit_population_Text2":"% / Staff"}

{"LHIN_Label_Text2":"Toronto Region","OrgCategory_Label_Text2":"Teaching Hospital","aim_header_Text2":"Patient-centred","comments2":"","current_value_text2":"27.00","datasource_period_Text2":"In house data collection  / April 1 2025- March 31, 2026","goal2":"1. Completion of Communication Plan by Q1 (April) 2. Fifty engagements with PE PowerBI dashboard within 2 weeks of Patient Experience Week 3. Deliver two presentations at 100% of eligible program council and committee meetings (Q1, Q3) 4. Identify four Champions (i.e. PCM, operations director, physician leader, Advanced Practice Nurse (APN))","measure_header_Text2":"The percentage of leaders that access the Patient Experience (PE)PowerBI dashboards per month based on the Ontario Hospital Association’s (OHA) digital patient experience surveys.","methods2":"Awareness and education of the PE PowerBI dashboards will be developed in collaboration with Sunnybrook’s Strategic Communications team where necessary. Awareness and education ‘campaign’: • Automated monthly emails sent to eligible organization leaders to check PE PowerBI Dashboard • Quarterly updates to organization leaders for internal and external benchmarking • Present at program council and other committee meetings across the organization to promote PE PowerBI dashboards • Identify PE Dashboard Champions to foster communication and engagement • Engage with PCMs and operations directors through small group or 1-on-1 sessions • Engage with Patient and Family Advisory Councils (PFACs) to promote dashboards","objective_header_Text2":"Experience","org_name_Text2":"Sunnybrook Health Sciences Centre","planned3":"Communications Plan/Promotion of PE PowerBI dashboards internally","process_measure3":"1. Completion of Communication Plan 2. Education campaign during Patient Experience Week (April 28 – May 2, 2025) 3. Number of presentations to promote dashboards 4. Number of PE Dashboard Champions","sector_name_Text2":"Acute Care/Hospital","target_justification2":"This indicator is a process measure. In order for patient experience data to effectively lead to improved patient safety and quality of care, the first step is to ensure that those able to effect change are receiving data and viewing the data. 

Therefore, the justification of the target is as a fidelity measure, we need to ensure that all leaders that have an available dashboard are viewing it – and if not, we need to understand why not – to better incorporate it into their workflow. 

Based on last year’s performance, the target of 75% is a stretch target, but anything below that will make it hard for the information available in the patient experience surveys to eventually lead to meaningful change.","target_value_text2":"75.00","unit_population_Text2":"% / Staff"}

{"LHIN_Label_Text2":"Toronto Region","OrgCategory_Label_Text2":"Teaching Hospital","aim_header_Text2":"Safe","comments2":"","current_value_text2":"32.80","datasource_period_Text2":"Other / April 1, 2025 March 31 2026","goal2":"70% of surveyed staff agree or strongly agree they can implement the 4M’s Greater than four communications focused on the 4 M’s (Mentation, Medication, What Matters, Mobility)","measure_header_Text2":"Enhance Safe Senior Friendly Care: Reduce delirium rate* for patients with Length of Stay (LOS) > 2 days and age =65*The Delirium rate is generated by the GEMINI Research Group using a computerized algorithm.","methods2":"Engage the Strategic Communications Team: to develop a plan to foster hospital-wide awareness and understanding of the IHI Age Friendly Designation though ongoing communication & profiling of this initiative.","objective_header_Text2":"Safety","org_name_Text2":"Sunnybrook Health Sciences Centre","planned3":"Increase Awareness of Institute for Healthcare Improvement (IHI) Age-Friendly Designation: Committed to Care Excellence 4 M’s • Mobilization • Mentation • What Matters • Medication","process_measure3":"Survey responses to gauge the level of awareness and ability to implement IHI’s Age Friendly 4M’s # of Communications on Sunnynet","sector_name_Text2":"Acute Care/Hospital","target_justification2":"Target (D2, D3, K3 East)

