{"LHIN_Label_Text2":"Toronto Region","OrgCategory_Label_Text2":"Teaching Hospital","aim_header_Text2":"Safe","comments2":"","current_value_text2":"32.80","datasource_period_Text2":"Other / April 1, 2025 March 31 2026","goal2":"1. 80% of patients with delirium have a Delirium Order Set completed during their admission in Q4 2025/26 2. 80% of staff on targeted units complete Micro-learnings by December, 2025 80% of staff on targeted units complete GPA training by December, 2025 3. Target TBD once baseline identified","measure_header_Text2":"Enhance Safe Senior Friendly Care: Reduce delirium rate* for patients with Length of Stay (LOS) > 2 days and age =65*The Delirium rate is generated by the GEMINI Research Group using a computerized algorithm.","methods2":"1. Delirium Order Sets: Review current practices related to Delirium Order Set use in eligible patients. Develop an awareness campaign and forcing functions (where applicable) to increase use of delirium order sets, which support the ordering and application of Senior Friendly and delirium management best practices. 2. LMS Learning Modules: Required staff to complete the following: • Delirium Micro-learning for Acute Care (3) • Managing Behaviours/Least Restraint Policy • Person-centred Language (PCL) • Gentle Persuasive Approaches (GPA) Training 3. Identify at-risk patients: • Implement interdepartmental team meetings to discuss complex cases and develop individualized prevention and treatment plans for patients at high-risk of delirium • Implement regular educational workshops/ online modules to educate healthcare providers on evidence-based strategies for preventing/managing delirium","objective_header_Text2":"Safety","org_name_Text2":"Sunnybrook Health Sciences Centre","planned3":"Mentation (Delirium): Improve knowledge and capacity of staff and physicians related to delirium prevention best practices **The change ideas under the Mentation heading will focus on the following four units: D2, D3, K3E, RCC","process_measure3":"1. % of patients with delirium reported at discharge (eDischarge) with a delirium order set completed 2. Percentage of staff who complete Micro-learning modules/ GPA Training 3. % of at-risk patients with a bundle of delirium reduction interventions in place (pharmacologic and non-pharmacologic)","sector_name_Text2":"Acute Care/Hospital","target_justification2":"Target (D2, D3, K3 East)

