{"LHIN_Label_Text2":"North West Region","OrgCategory_Label_Text2":"Teaching Hospital","aim_header_Text2":"Equitable","comments2":"Executive-level target has been removed as 100% achieved in last QIP.","current_value_text2":"26.54","datasource_period_Text2":"Local data collection / Other","goal2":"Progress for process measure will be an increase in each quarter until target is reached.","measure_header_Text2":"Percentage of staff (executive-level, management, or all) who have completed relevant equity, diversity, inclusion, and anti-racism education","methods2":"1) Staff: Traditional Wellness Lead, Interprofessional Educator. 2) Offer various forms of cultural safety and other relevant EDI training to all staff during orientation and monthly RSC sessions. 3) Develop a plan with Human Resources to identify other funding sources to support and enable participation of previous frontline staff.","objective_header_Text2":"Equity","org_name_Text2":"Thunder Bay Regional Hlth Sciences Ctr","planned3":"SP2026 has an EDI initiative to implement Cultural Safety and other relevant EDI training within the organization.","process_measure3":"1) Ensure staffing is maintained. 2) Track % of staff (broken down by Management and General Staff) who have completed relevant training.","sector_name_Text2":"Acute Care/Hospital","target_justification2":"Internal SP2026 Cultural Safety Training Core Team set reasonable targets for Management and General Staff based on the capacity of the Traditional Wellness Lead and Elders. Target is completion of "Repairing the Sacred Circle" (RSC) as part of comprehensive, regionally specific training.

Note: Current performance is 98% Managerial and 23% General Staff. Unable to enter this data in the respective section. A total of 129 out of 131 Managers completed the training, along with 821 out of 3448 General Staff. 

Note: Targets are 95% Managerial and 25% General Staff. Unable to enter this data in the respective section.","target_value_text2":"25.00","unit_population_Text2":"% / Staff"}

{"LHIN_Label_Text2":"East Region","OrgCategory_Label_Text2":"Large Community Hospital","aim_header_Text2":"Timely","comments2":"","current_value_text2":"CB","datasource_period_Text2":"EMR/Chart Review / 2026/2027","goal2":"100%: current-state versus future-state review is completed.","measure_header_Text2":"ED Wait Time Efficiencies","methods2":"Conduct a current-state versus future-state workflow review to understand how Epic may impact ED wait time efficiencies and data capture.","objective_header_Text2":"Access and Flow","org_name_Text2":"Pembroke Regional Hospital Inc.","planned3":"Understand impacts of Epic on ED workflows in preparation for October 2026 Go-Live.","process_measure3":"Current-state versus future-state review completed.","sector_name_Text2":"Acute Care/Hospital","target_justification2":"Efficient Emergency Department flow is essential to patient safety, timely access to care, and overall patient experience. Excessive wait times, whether for initial assessment or overall length of stay, contribute to treatment delays, overcrowding, increased patient dissatisfaction, and higher rates of patients leaving without being seen.

In 2026/27, Pembroke Regional Hospital (PRH) will be implementing a new electronic health record system (Epic) that will substantially change workflows/processes across our entire organization. While Epic is expected, ultimately, to improve efficiencies, data accuracy, and team communication over time, there are inherent short-term risks during implementation that may negatively affect ED performance. Prioritizing early stabilization is essential to maintaining safe and reliable care for patients.

Given the above, PRH's primary aim for this 26/27 QIP is to support safe and stable Emergency Department operations throughout Epic implementation. Post Epic Go-Live, PRH will be investing in Lean resources within our ED to support the application of Lean methodologies to identify and implement opportunities for improvement of wait time metrics, while also positioning us for further improvements in subsequent QIP cycles.","target_value_text2":"CB","unit_population_Text2":"Hours / ED patients"}

