{"LHIN_Label_Text2":"East Region","OrgCategory_Label_Text2":"Small Hospital","aim_header_Text2":"Timely","comments2":"","current_value_text2":"40.00","datasource_period_Text2":"CIHI NACRS / Other","goal2":"100% of months with scorecard review and documented discussion (as required)","measure_header_Text2":"90th percentile ambulance offload time","methods2":"- Keep Ambulance Offload Time on the ED Scorecard. - Present and discuss results at ED Quality Meetings. - Record any follow-up actions (e.g., escalation triggers, workflow reinforcement, partner outreach to EMS) in meeting notes. Share a brief summary of actions at huddles to close the feedback loop.","objective_header_Text2":"Access and Flow","org_name_Text2":"Arnprior Regional Health","planned3":"Maintain visibility and early‑warning oversight of ambulance offload performance through routine ED Scorecard monitoring and leadership review.","process_measure3":"Percentage of months in which the Ambulance Offload indicator appears on the ED Scorecard and is reviewed at ED Quality Meetings.","sector_name_Text2":"Acute Care/Hospital","target_justification2":"ARH has selected a 36‑minute ambulance offload target with a stretch-goal to reach a target of 30 mins by Q4.

Although ambitious, this target is justified by the significant work completed last fiscal year to improve data integrity and ensure offload times accurately reflect ED operations. With strengthened auditing processes and improved documentation practices, the ED team is confident in our ability to progress toward this benchmark.

Challenges and risks: The transition to a new EHR (EPIC) in October will require a reset of our data quality processes and substantial workflow realignment. Staff will require focused coaching to ensure documentation continues to accurately captures the patient journey. Additionally, the absence of a Business Intelligence tool means data validation will continue to require considerable manual effort. These risks inform our mitigation strategies but do not change our commitment to pursuing the 36 min target with a stretch target of 30 min.","target_value_text2":"36.00","unit_population_Text2":"Minutes / Patients"}

{"LHIN_Label_Text2":"East Region","OrgCategory_Label_Text2":"Small Hospital","aim_header_Text2":"Timely","comments2":"","current_value_text2":"40.00","datasource_period_Text2":"CIHI NACRS / Other","goal2":"Ensure TOC is documented and completed for F2S patients by auditing 4 F2S patient charts per quarter. There will be no specific target for this activity this year given this is a new program. We will monitor the utilization and co-develop standard work for TOC with a goal of setting KPI's for this program for the following FY.","measure_header_Text2":"90th percentile ambulance offload time","methods2":"Continue to work with region on co-development of standards of practice (SOP) to ensure safe and timely TOC in the ED mainwaiting room (MWR).","objective_header_Text2":"Access and Flow","org_name_Text2":"Arnprior Regional Health","planned3":"Partner with paramedic service in Renfrew County to implement Fit2Sit program. Program includes rapid offload of stable patients who meet specific criteria to the ED waiting room/seated care area, enabling earlier transfer of care (TOC) for paramedics.","process_measure3":"Monitor # of Fit2Sit patients offloaded to MWR monthly in addition to ensuring TOC is appropriately captured on this patient population.","sector_name_Text2":"Acute Care/Hospital","target_justification2":"ARH has selected a 36‑minute ambulance offload target with a stretch-goal to reach a target of 30 mins by Q4.

Although ambitious, this target is justified by the significant work completed last fiscal year to improve data integrity and ensure offload times accurately reflect ED operations. With strengthened auditing processes and improved documentation practices, the ED team is confident in our ability to progress toward this benchmark.

Challenges and risks: The transition to a new EHR (EPIC) in October will require a reset of our data quality processes and substantial workflow realignment. Staff will require focused coaching to ensure documentation continues to accurately captures the patient journey. Additionally, the absence of a Business Intelligence tool means data validation will continue to require considerable manual effort. These risks inform our mitigation strategies but do not change our commitment to pursuing the 36 min target with a stretch target of 30 min.","target_value_text2":"36.00","unit_population_Text2":"Minutes / Patients"}

