Although ambitious, this target is justified by the significant work completed last fiscal year to improve data integrity and ensure offload times accurately reflect ED operations. With strengthened auditing processes and improved documentation practices, the ED team is confident in our ability to progress toward this benchmark.

Challenges and risks: The transition to a new EHR (EPIC) in October will require a reset of our data quality processes and substantial workflow realignment. Staff will require focused coaching to ensure documentation continues to accurately captures the patient journey. Additionally, the absence of a Business Intelligence tool means data validation will continue to require considerable manual effort. These risks inform our mitigation strategies but do not change our commitment to pursuing the 36 min target with a stretch target of 30 min.","target_value_text2":"36.00","unit_population_Text2":"Minutes / Patients"}

{"LHIN_Label_Text2":"Toronto Region","OrgCategory_Label_Text2":"Teaching Hospital","aim_header_Text2":"Efficient","comments2":"","current_value_text2":"48.30","datasource_period_Text2":"In-home audit / FY 2025-26","goal2":"Complete chart audit and root cause analysis for non-indicated telemetry use.","measure_header_Text2":"Choosing Wisely telemetryObjective: Decrease use of non-indicated continuous cardiac monitoring (telemetry) per American Heart Association (AHA) guidelines in patients admitted to ward beds excluding ICU patients and D3 patients at Bayview Campus.Indicator: Proportion of patients for whom telemetry is ordered and initiated without an appropriate indication per AHA guidelines, or who are on telemetry longer than the indicated duration.","methods2":"A physician-led chart audit will be completed to establish a baseline understanding of the frequency and duration of non-indicated telemetry use by end of April 2026. We will then perform a root cause analysis to determine drivers of this problem.","objective_header_Text2":"Access and Flow","org_name_Text2":"Sunnybrook Health Sciences Centre","planned3":"Establish a baseline for inappropriate/non-indicated telemetry use through retrospective chart review","process_measure3":"Proportion and duration of non-indicated telemetry use among hospitalized, ward patients. Proportion of patients admitted in the ED who are designated for a ward bed but cannot go to the ward owing to lack of availability of a telemetry pack","sector_name_Text2":"Acute Care/Hospital","target_justification2":"Current Performance: Sunnybrook’s inappropriate telemetry rate based on six month chart review (March – August 2025): 48.3% (293/606)

